    <span class="eyebrow"><em>Variola major</em> · the only human disease ever eradicated</span>
    <h1 class="disp">The <span class="light">one disease</span><br><span class="gold">we ever beat.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Smallpox killed on a scale almost nothing else has — roughly a third of everyone it infected, and more people in the 20th century than every war of that century combined. Then, for the only time in human history, a coordinated global campaign made a disease disappear. It did not happen by accident, and it did not stay finished quite as cleanly as the record likes to say.</p>
